    "verdict": "INCONCLUSIVE for basis capability: the signed (hollow-capable) basis produced a converged force-balanced equilibrium on only 0/16 slices (vs 16/16 for the frozen non-negative basis), even warm-started from the frozen solution. Non-negativity is load-bearing for solver convergence; a classical basis swap is not an available fix \u2014 the ramp-phase profile freedom must come from the learned operator / temporal supervision, not by relaxing the classical basis."
