  "verdicts": {
    "H1_profile_basis_inadequacy": {
      "supported": "STRONG (primary)",
      "evidence": "boundary error tracks the fit's own inability to satisfy the magnetics: cost-vs-LCFS Spearman r=0.57 (p=1.6e-12) overall, within-ramp r=0.77; peak error and peak cost coincide in the limited->diverted transition band, not at lowest Ip. The residual is a shape+position error the static peaked basis leaves behind: |a1| horizontal shift 4.0 cm and |a2| elongation 5.7 cm (both signed and ~4-6x the flat-top level), plus a large scattered size error |a0|=5.9 cm. The frozen non-negative monomial basis cannot represent a hollow ramp-phase j_phi, so it settles on a wrong interior that still fits the sensors."
    },
    "H2_signal_snr_floor": {
      "supported": "REJECTED",
      "evidence": "error does NOT rise monotonically as Ip falls: the lowest-Ip bin (Ip-frac<0.6) has among the LOWEST error and lowest fit cost, while the peak error and cost sit in the limited->diverted transition band (Ip-frac 0.75-0.85). A noise/SNR floor would make the lowest-Ip slices worst; they are not. LCFS-vs-Ip Spearman only r=-0.37."
    },
    "H3_boundary_read_topology": {
      "supported": "REJECTED (no misclassification)",
      "evidence": "ramp-up slices are LIMITED in both spine and referee (model diverted frac 0.16, referee 0.40, topology-class agreement 0.67); the gap is in the limited boundary SHAPE, not the limited/diverted class. (In the transition band the spine does UNDER-form the X-point EFIT reads \u2014 a symptom of the same too-round boundary, not an independent read bug.)"
    },
    "H4_referee_quality": {
      "supported": "MINOR contributor",
      "evidence": "EFIT LCFS mean-radius slew 0.082 cm/ms on ramp vs 0.012 flat-top (~7x), i.e. ~1.9 cm per 23 ms label step \u2014 real and partly genuine plasma growth, but small vs the 5.5 cm ramp-flat gap."
    },
    "H5_shape_dynamics": {
      "supported": "STRONG (is the H1 signature)",
      "evidence": "the ramp residual is broad-band shape+position: elongation harmonic |a2| 5.7 cm (signed +5.7) and horizontal shift |a1| 4.0 cm (signed -3.8), vs 3.2/0.9 cm flat-top. The static disc prior + peaked basis fixes a shape that lags the fast-elongating, inboard-limited ramp plasma EFIT resolves."
    }
